          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why is osteoarthritis not simply “wear and tear” of a joint?",
          "answer": "Osteoarthritis is not simply wear and tear. The main reference describes it as a disorder of the whole joint, not just the cartilage. Cartilage is progressively lost, the bone underneath remodels in response, and the process involves inflammation and attempted repair (*Osteoarthritis*, General clinical reference). Because it is active, resting the joint is not the answer. Muscle weakness that follows reduced use can make the joint worse.\n\nThis is why exercise is the first-line treatment. The rheumatology and orthopedic guidance places exercise ahead of medicines, which are described as add-ons (*Osteoarthritis: exercise-first management*). The exercise program combines strengthening of the muscles around the joint, range-of-movement work, and aerobic activity (*Exercising with osteoarthritis*).\n\nI could not get passages on the role of genetics, age, and mechanical load. My search for those returned an error because the tool-call limit was reached, so I cannot explain them from the sources here. A clinician or a reliable medical resource can cover them. I have not filled that gap from memory.\n\nIf you have joint pain, a doctor can assess it and discuss a plan that suits you.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
